# Remove sender attribution and empty host lines from invitations

byre task tskfuvVTqoTkmc, "Fix invitation wording", created by ian@fc.run, merged by ian@fc.run.
Full chats: the events of task tskfuvVTqoTkmc in byre (read_task_events with task_id tskfuvVTqoTkmc).

## Summary

Fixed When invitation wording after reproducing the hostless output in both email formats.

Before: Hostless invitation and detail-update emails included a bare “Hosted by” line.
Now: Text and HTML include the host line only when hosts exist, preserving names for hosted events.

Before: Invitation and detail-update bodies named the person who sent them.
Now: Per Ian’s explicit request, invitations say “You're invited to” and detail updates say “The details have been updated for”, without sender attribution, including when a member invites a guest.

Focused regression tests cover hosted and hostless invitations and updates in both formats; queued-delivery tests pass. A sample rendered email was previewed. Review’s scope finding was dismissed based on Ian’s explicit instruction. Main was already up to date when the final merge was requested. Other message types, mail headers, and calendar organizer behavior were outside scope.

